    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d647">

                <pb facs="0731" n="651" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg651"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Powell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-09-10"><hi rendition="#italic">September 10,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 538.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 1140, of the 29th ultimo, in regard to the political situation in Haiti.</p>
                <p>Your communication to the Provisional Government advising it that this Government
                    would not recognize a paper blockade of Gonaives, St. Marc, and Port de Paix,
                    nor one imposed without due notice given, is approved.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
